*** Resetting replication at the very beginning of the test.

*** Generating a configuration file in JSON format for the Binlog
*** Server utility.

*** Determining binlog file directory from the server.

*** Creating a temporary directory <BINSRV_STORAGE_PATH> for storing
*** binlog files downloaded via the Binlog Server utility.

*** Determining the first binary log name.

*** Creating a table with a MEDIUMBLOB column.
CREATE DATABASE source_db;
CREATE TABLE source_db.tbl(
id INT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,
data MEDIUMBLOB NOT NULL,
PRIMARY KEY(id)
) ENGINE=InnoDB;

*** Inserting 20 rows of ~100 KiB each. The cumulative row-based
*** event stream reliably straddles multiple 1 MiB PBS fetch blocks,
*** so most blocks end mid-event and leave a partial-event tail that
*** sender_context must carry over to the next fetch instead of
*** re-reading it from storage. Individual events stay well under
*** 1 MiB, so the oversize-event path is not exercised here -- this
*** isolates tail reuse.

*** Fetching the source binary logs into PBS storage.

*** Starting Binlog Server Utility in background in pull mode.
include/read_file_to_var.inc

*** Waiting for the replication source listener port ready to
*** accept connections.

*** Dumping the binary logs from the Binlog Server replication
*** source. --stop-never is NOT set, so PBS disconnects on EOF
*** once it has streamed everything in storage.

*** Waiting for the tail-reuse log entry in the PBS log. Its
*** presence confirms sender_context carried partial-event bytes
*** from a prior fetch and prepended them to the next fetch,
*** instead of re-reading those bytes from storage.
include/wait_for_pattern_in_file.inc [sender : reusing]

*** Sending SIGTERM signal to the Binlog Server Utility and
*** waiting for the process to terminate.

*** Moving source_db.tbl to backup_db.tbl.
CREATE DATABASE backup_db;
RENAME TABLE source_db.tbl TO backup_db.tbl;
DROP DATABASE source_db;

*** Restoring source_db from the PBS-served dump.

*** Comparing the restored and backup rows via an order-independent
*** per-row signature. BIT_XOR of CRC32 over (id, length, MD5(data))
*** fits in a single BIGINT and avoids both GROUP_CONCAT limits and
*** sort-buffer sizing for the ~2 MiB total blob payload.

*** Dropping the round-trip databases.
DROP DATABASE source_db;
DROP DATABASE backup_db;

*** Removing the Binlog Server utility storage directory.

*** Removing the Binlog Server utility log file.

*** Removing the Binlog Server utility configuration file.
